- trade <player>: exchange an equal number of resources with them.
- bribe <player>: give 2 resources to potentially get a stronger negotiation position.
- negotiate <player>: propose a trade for 3 resources if you are not currently proposing. If the proposal is accepted, both gain the proposed trade amount.

At the end of each round, all players vote to decide if someone should be penalized for excessive negotiations or trading. Players can either support or oppose the penalty on any given round.

Bribery allows players to temporarily influence negotiations to their advantage, but comes with risks. Excessive negotiation can lead to penalties, so players must balance resource accumulation with strategic decisions.
