An explorer is considered potentially plundering if they have taken from a grove before and not been warned.
Only an explorer with at least 1 seed can issue a warning.

If an explorer issues a warning and a potential plunderer plunders, the potential plunderer loses all their seeds. The warning prevents other explorers from plundering the grove during the current turn.

Players can choose to guard a grove during their turn, which protects that grove from being plundered. However, issuing a warning uses up one turn, so it cannot be used immediately after gathering seeds.
