RULES = """
Mutant Clones. 3 players, 10 rounds, one move each per round.
- mutate: create a new clone that duplicates your stash. Your existing stash has +1 resource.
- clone: use a clone to replicate your stash into an adjacent player. The clone disappears.
- sacrifice: eliminate a player from the game by giving them all your resources. No cost.
- recruit: steal resources from the bystanders to join the game (cost is twice this amount). The game ends.
- sabotage: attempt to sabotage a player without cloning them. If successful, the target player loses 1 resource; otherwise, you lose 2 resources.

Each player starts with 3 resources and 2 clones. Resources exceeding 0 are lost in rounds where no action is taken.
The last player to remain in the game wins.
"""

import random

class Game:
    def __init__(self, n_players, endowments, bystanders, seed):
        assert n_players == 3
        self.n = n_players; self.res = list(endowments); self.bys = list(bystanders)
        self.turn = 0; self.rounds = 10; self.clones = 2

    def to_move(self): return self.turn % self.n

    def legal_moves(self, p):
        if self.res[p] == 0:
            return ["sacrifice", "recruit"]
        moves = ["mutate", "clone"] + (["sabotage"] if self.turn > 0 else [])
        return moves

    def play(self, p, move):
        w = move.split(" ")
        if w[0] == "mutate":
            if self.res[p] > 0:
                self.res[p] += 1; self.clones += 1
        elif w[0] == "clone":
            if self.clones > 0:
                q = self.to_move()
                if q != p and self.res[q - 1] > 0:
                    self.res[q] = self.res[p]
                    self.clones -= 1
                    if q % 2 == 0:
                        self.res[q] -= 1
        elif w[0] == "sacrifice":
            if self.res[p] > 0:
                q = self.to_move()
                if q != p:
                    for r in range(self.n):
                        self.res[r] = 0
        elif w[0] == "recruit":
            if self.res[self.to_move()] < len(self.bys):
                i = int(w[1])
                if self.bys[i] > 0:
                    self.res[p] += self.bys[i]
                    self.bys[i] = 0
        elif w[0] == "sabotage":
            if self.turn > 0:
                victim = ((self.to_move() + 1) % self.n)
                if self.res[victim] > 0:
                    self.res[victim] -= 1
                else:
                    self.res[self.to_move()] -= 2
        for res in self.res:
            if res <= 0:
                self.res[self.to_move()] = 0
        self.turn += 1

    def describe(self, p):
        return (
            f"Round {self.turn}. "
            f"Your stash: {self.res[p]}; Clones: {self.clones}, available for action."
        )

    def over(self):
        return all(res == 0 for res in self.res) or self.turn >= self.rounds
    def final_resources(self): return list(self.res)
    def final_bystanders(self): return list(self.bys)

RULES = """
In this Resource Exchange game, there are three players: Alice (A), Bob (B), and Carol (C). They start with 10 items each. Their goal is to maximize their individual scores by trading items with each other. At every turn, each player can either exchange items with their immediate neighbor (B or C) or with the bystanders (A and B), depending on whether the items they need are available in those locations.

